00:00:17.072 --> 00:00:21.043
STONEMAN DOUGLAS.

00:00:17.973 --> 00:00:22.678
AND THAT IS THE FBI AT WORK.

00:00:21.176 --> 00:00:23.846
STILL A CRIME SCENE, OF COURSE.

00:00:22.811 --> 00:00:29.051
AND WE JUST HAD CONFIRMATION IF

00:00:23.979 --> 00:00:30.252
YOU ARE JUST TUNING IN THAT

00:00:29.185 --> 00:00:33.556
APPARENTLY THE BODIES REMAIN

00:00:30.386 --> 00:00:32.588
INSIDE THE SCHOOL, UNFORTUNATELY

00:00:32.588 --> 00:00:33.989
INSIDE THE SCHOOL, UNFORTUNATEL

00:00:33.689 --> 00:00:36.692
UNFORTUNATELY.

00:00:34.123 --> 00:00:37.393
GEORGE IS A STUDENT AT MARJORY

00:00:36.826 --> 00:00:38.627
STONEMAN DOUGLAS HIGH SCHOOL,

00:00:37.526 --> 00:00:42.431
JOINING US BY PHONE.

00:00:38.761 --> 00:00:45.334
SO YOU KNEW NIKOLAS CRUZ?

00:00:42.565 --> 00:00:45.968
&gt;&gt; YES, I HAD MET HIM.

00:00:45.468 --> 00:00:47.903
&gt;&gt; Tucker: WHAT WAS YOUR

00:00:46.102 --> 00:00:53.009
IMPRESSION OF HIM?

00:00:48.037 --> 00:00:54.510
&gt;&gt; HE WAS ALWAYS A TROUBLEMAKER.

00:00:53.142 --> 00:00:58.447
HE WAS ALWAYS THE CLASS CLOWN,

00:00:54.644 --> 00:00:59.415
AND ALWAYS TRIED TO MAKE PEOPLE

00:00:58.581 --> 00:01:02.251
LAUGH IN THE CLASSROOM AND WOULD

00:00:59.549 --> 00:01:04.487
ALWAYS DO BAD THINGS.

00:01:02.385 --> 00:01:07.223
&gt;&gt; Tucker: WHAT KIND OF BAD

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:10.393
THINGS?

00:01:07.356 --> 00:01:14.697
&gt;&gt; HE WOULD JUST MAKE COMMENTS

00:01:10.526 --> 00:01:15.798
TO THE TEACHER AND MESS AROUND,

00:01:14.831 --> 00:01:18.534
BASED ON RANDOM THINGS.

00:01:15.932 --> 00:01:22.271
&gt;&gt; Tucker: CAN YOU GIVE US AN

00:01:18.668 --> 00:01:24.373
EXAMPLE?

00:01:22.405 --> 00:01:30.079
&gt;&gt; I REMEMBER EIGHTH GRADE ONE

00:01:24.507 --> 00:01:33.916
TIME WHEN THE TEACHER -- HE WENT

00:01:30.213 --> 00:01:37.320
ON THE TEACHERS COMPUTER AND

00:01:35.785 --> 00:01:38.288
STARTED LOOKING UP THINGS AND

00:01:37.453 --> 00:01:44.093
THEN WHEN THE TEACHER WALKED

00:01:38.421 --> 00:01:47.030
BACK INTO THE CLASSROOM HE JUST

00:01:44.227 --> 00:01:48.398
GOT AWAY FROM THE LAPTOP.

00:01:47.163 --> 00:01:49.465
&gt;&gt; Tucker: HE WAS EXPELLED

00:01:48.531 --> 00:01:52.335
FROM HIGH SCHOOL WE HAVE BEEN

00:01:49.599 --> 00:01:52.702
TOLD, DO YOU KNOW WHY HE WAS

00:01:52.468 --> 00:01:54.137
EXPELLED?

00:01:52.835 --> 00:01:58.208
&gt;&gt; NO, I DO NOT HAVE ANY

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:59.275
INFORMATION ON THAT.

00:01:58.341 --> 00:02:01.277
&gt;&gt; Tucker: WITHOUT VIOLATING

00:01:59.409 --> 00:02:04.514
THE PRIVACY OF ANYONE, BUT WHAT

00:02:01.411 --> 00:02:06.916
WAS HIS FAMILY SITUATION LIKE?

00:02:04.647 --> 00:02:11.855
&gt;&gt; I REALLY DID NOT KNOW.

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:12.455
AFTER EIGHTH GRADE, WE WENT OUR

00:02:11.988 --> 00:02:14.958
SEPARATE WAYS.

00:02:12.589 --> 00:02:15.859
I HAD NOT REALLY TALKED TO HIM

00:02:15.091 --> 00:02:18.294
SINCE.

00:02:15.992 --> 00:02:19.262
&gt;&gt; Tucker: WHEN HE SAW HIS

00:02:18.428 --> 00:02:20.330
NAME THIS AFTERNOON IN

00:02:19.396 --> 00:02:22.599
CONNECTION WITH THIS MASS

00:02:20.463 --> 00:02:24.434
SHOOTING, WHAT WAS YOUR FIRST

00:02:22.732 --> 00:02:25.368
RESPONSE?

00:02:24.568 --> 00:02:28.038
&gt;&gt; HONESTLY, I DID NOT REALLY

00:02:25.502 --> 00:02:29.873
KNOW HOW TO REACT.

00:02:28.172 --> 00:02:32.776
I KNEW THAT HE WAS BAD, BUT I

00:02:30.007 --> 00:02:33.177
DID NOT KNOW THAT HE WAS THIS

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:33.810
BAD.

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:36.313
&gt;&gt; Tucker: IT SOUNDS LIKE

00:02:35.145 --> 00:02:38.916
NOBODY DID.

00:02:36.446 --> 00:02:40.117
BUT YOU WERE NOT TOTALLY SHOCKED

00:02:39.049 --> 00:02:48.825
THEN?

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:51.762
&gt;&gt; I MEAN, I WAS SHOCKED.

00:02:48.959 --> 00:02:52.095
ALL I CAN SAY IS THAT I WAS

00:02:51.895 --> 00:02:55.866
SHOCKED.

